The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (unlikely(copied < len && !PageUptodate(page))) {
    copied = 0;
    goto out;
```
Reason:
This logic prevents the page from being marked as uptodate when the amount of data copied is less than the length specified, even if the write operation was successful. As a result, pages can remain marked as not uptodate, leading to potential data integrity issues.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!PageUptodate(page)) {
    if (unlikely(copied < len)) {
        copied = 0;
        goto out;
    } else if (len == PAGE_SIZE) {
        SetPageUptodate(page);
    }
}
```
Reason:
This modification allows the page to be marked as uptodate if the entire page size is written successfully, thus ensuring that the page reflects the correct state after a successful write operation. This change addresses the root cause of the bug by properly updating the page status when the correct amount of data is written.

